<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yahdun-Lim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1800 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yahdun-Lim was an Amorite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a> around 1800 BCE. He subdued the pastoral tribes of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, founded fortresses and led an expedition to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, where, according to his foundation inscription, he washed his weapons in the sea. He was murdered in a palace coup, Mari soon fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamshi-adad-i">Shamshi-Adad I</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimri-lim">Zimri-Lim</a> later claimed descent from him.</p></div>
